messages:
maria: Quick check — I'm about to land a Terraform change that enables mixed spot/on-demand for the GPU ASG. Wanted to make sure autoscaler headroom and podAnnotations are correct before I push.

maria: Current plan: create aws_autoscaling_group with mixed_instances_policy, reserve 1 on-demand for control, spot for scale. Terraform snippet: 
```hcl
resource "aws_autoscaling_group" "gpu-asg" {
  mixed_instances_policy {
    instances_distribution {
      on_demand_percentage_above_base_capacity = 20
      spot_allocation_strategy = "capacity-optimized"
    }
    launch_template {
      launch_template_specification {
        id = aws_launch_template.gpu.id
      }
    }
  }
  min_size = 0
  max_size = 50
  desired_capacity = 4
}
```

maria: And cluster-autoscaler needs the nodegroup label and annotation so it ignores short-lived spot churn. Thinking: annotate nodes with `cluster-autoscaler.kubernetes.io/scale-down-disabled: "false"` and taint `gpu=dedicated:NoSchedule` for reserved on-demand. Any objections?

jason: small nit: on_demand_percentage_above_base_capacity is percent of base, not absolute — if base_capacity=1 and percentage 20 you'll still only get 1 on-demand. set base_capacity to 1 and percentage to 100 if you want 1 guaranteed on-demand always. or explicitly use overrides + weighted_capacity.

alisa: for cluster-autoscaler, we should set the expander and priorities. Add this to the ASG tags: 
`k8s.io/cluster-autoscaler/enabled=true`
`k8s.io/cluster-autoscaler/gpu-asg=true`
and in CA flags use `--skip-nodes-with-local-storage=false --expander=least-waste` to prefer spot.

kevin: also watch kubelet eviction thresholds when spot drains — pods with large PVs might get killed. For GPUs it's usually fine but we should add pod disruption budgets on long-running jobs.

maria: noted. What about secrets wiring? The GPU nodes need access to the license key from secrets manager and we mount via KMS-encrypted SSM param. Terraform currently adds IAM to the node role: 
```hcl
resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "node-secrets" {
  role = aws_iam_role.node_role.id
  policy = jsonencode({
    Statement = [{
      Action = ["ssm:GetParameter", "secretsmanager:GetSecretValue"],
      Effect = "Allow",
      Resource = "arn:aws:ssm:us-west-2:123456789012:parameter/gpu-license*"
    }]
  })
}
```

jason: fine but limit to the specific secrets and include condition for `kms:ViaService` to reduce blast radius.

infra-bot: deploy-check: terraform plan passed in staging cluster (plan sha: b3f9c). No drift detected.

alisa: One more thing — set `spot_interruption_behavior=terminate` in the ASG so cluster-autoscaler sees the node gone quickly. Also add a lifecycle hook if we want graceful eviction.

maria: thanks all — I'll update the TF with jason's base_capacity/percentage fix, tighten the IAM per jason, add CA tags per alisa, and set interruption_behavior. Will open a PR and ping @eng-oncall for an extra review. CC: @kevin for PDB guidance. :thumbsup:

kevin: :eyes: ping me when PR is up, I'll check PDBs and eviction handler config.

maria: PR opened — 1779123499 — links to plan in staging and includes lifecycle hook + small script to drain GPUs gracefully.

jason: looked — left one comment on launch_template userdata (missing `--enable-kubelet-eviction`). Otherwise LGTM.

maria: addressed comment, updated userdata, re-ran plan, bumping last_message_ts. thanks everyone.
